UnitDeployRelayStack
├── when parameters are not valid
│   ├── when the chain id does not match the current chain
│   │   └── it should revert with ChainIdMismatch
│   ├── when the voting escrow is the zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidInput
│   ├── when the payments module is the zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidInput
│   ├── when the voter is the zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidInput
│   └── when the governor is the zero address
│       └── it should revert with InvalidInput
├── when the shipped parameters are still placeholders
│   └── it should revert rather than deploy a stack bound to nothing
├── when no other deployment unit has run
│   └── it should deploy every contract at its deterministic create three address
├── when the pools unit ran first under the same deployer
│   ├── it should deploy every contract at its deterministic create three address
│   └── it should leave the pool unit addresses untouched
└── when reading the relay entropies against the deployment registry
    └── it should share no entropy with another deployment unit
